# run_gate.py — fail-closed completeness gate

`python3 tools/run_gate.py runs/<date>_<game>/ [--now 2026-11-01T12:00]`
Exit 0 = PASS, 1 = FAIL. Prints report (paste at top of report.md) and writes `<run_dir>/gate_output.txt`.
Tests: `cd tools/tests && python3 -m unittest -v test_run_gate` (fixture regenerated by `make_fixture.py`).

## Run folder must contain
- `checklist.md` — table `| Leg | Phase | Status | Number | Source | Pulled (ET) |`. Phase cell starts with the phase number (1–15). One row per phase per leg; leg text must equal manifest `legs[].name`. Non-N/A rows need a source and a parseable `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM` ET time.
- `report.md`
- `run_manifest.json`:
```json
{
 "game": "TEN@CIN", "kickoff_et": "2026-11-01T13:00",
 "sources": [{"category": "core_stats_pbp|coverage_matchups|ngs|film|injuries_news|weather|odds_props",
              "name": "fanduel", "url_or_file": "https://... or /path", "pulled_et": "2026-11-01T11:30", "tool": "firecrawl|curl|..."}],
 "flagged_gaps": [{"category": "ngs", "reason": "blocked 403"}],
 "pressure_inputs": {"blitz_rate": {"value": 0.3, "source": "...", "pulled_et": "..."},
                     "pressure_rate": {...,"label": "PROXY"}, "checkdown_share": {...}},
 "sims": [{"model": "monte_carlo|bias|game_randomness", "n": 100000, "seed": 42,
           "legs": {"<leg name>": {"p": 0.58, "median": 64}}}],
 "legs": [{"name": "<leg name>", "type": "WR|TE|RB|QB", "receiving": true, "status": "PASS|CUT",
           "side": "over|under", "line": 58.5, "no_vig": 0.52, "gaps": [],
           "coverage": {"defenders": [{"name": "...", "targets": 40, "comp_pct": 0.6, "ypt": 7.1, "source": "...", "pulled_et": "..."}],
                        "man_zone": {"man": 0.3, "zone": 0.7, "source": "...", "pulled_et": "..."},
                        "mof": {"open": 0.45, "closed": 0.55, "source": "...", "pulled_et": "..."}}}]
}
```
Times are ET, naive ISO (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM`). Set `receiving: true` for WR/TE and RB receiving or rush+rec legs.

## Fails if
- any phase 1–15 row missing for any leg; unknown status; row without source/time
- any of the 7 categories has no source with url_or_file and a fresh timestamp
- staleness: coverage_matchups (incl. defender, man/zone, MOF, pressure inputs) > 48 h; injuries_news > 6 h; odds_props > 1 h; else > 48 h; unknown time = stale
- live receiving leg lacks defenders (targets, comp_pct, ypt), man_zone or mof
- blitz_rate / pressure_rate / checkdown_share missing
- any model missing, n < 100000, no seed, or no p/median for a live leg
- edge rule on a live leg: avg(p)−no_vig ≥ .03; 0.5+0.7(avg p−0.5)−no_vig > 0; every model p ≥ .45; every model median clears the line for the side
- Gaps: a checklist row FAIL/MISSING/STALE/UNVERIFIED or non-empty `gaps` is allowed only if the leg `status` is CUT. A missing category is allowed only if listed in `flagged_gaps` AND every leg is CUT. CUT legs skip sim/coverage/edge checks.

## Approved exceptions (staleness waiver, coverage.defenders only)
Manifest fields: `game_date` (YYYY-MM-DD; falls back to the date of `kickoff_et`) and
```json
"approved_exceptions": [{"input": "coverage.defenders", "source": "/workspace/nfl-sim/mnf12/pfr_def_adv_2026.html",
  "approved_by": "Rico", "approved_on": "2026-11-01", "valid_for_date": "2026-11-01", "scope": "receiving legs",
  "reason": "..."}]
```
- An exception applies only when `input` is `coverage.defenders`, all fields are present, and `valid_for_date == game_date`. The defender entry's `source` must match the exception's `source` (by file name), and it still needs a parseable `pulled_et`.
- When it applies, only that defender's 48 h staleness check is skipped. Man/zone, MOF, pressure inputs, injuries, odds and sims are never waived. On any other date the exception is ignored (logged under Notes) and the 48 h rule fails the input.
- Every applied exception is printed under `APPROVED EXCEPTIONS:` in the gate output.
- report.md must have a heading containing "Risks" whose section names each applied exception's source file (e.g. `pfr_def_adv_2026.html`), or the gate fails.

## Recent form (BUG-2026-11-01-FORM) — every live (non-CUT) leg
`legs[].recent_form = {values:[…], games:[game_id…], qb, source, pulled_et}` — values from real box scores / pbp only
(nflverse pbp or ESPN). Missing/no source/no qb/stale (core_stats_pbp limit)/values≠games/<3 games → FAIL (closed).
- §7 HARD: leg must clear its exact line in ≥3 of last 4 (or 3 of 3) with the current QB; for unders the under must hit.
- §14 yards overs only (passyds, recyds, rushyds, rushrec): needs `price`/`price_fd` (missing → FAIL).
  ≤-150: last-4 median ≥ 1.20×line. -113…-149: median ≥ 1.25×line AND ≥3 of 4 values ≥ 1.10×line. Shorter/plus money: note only.
- Fill helper: runs/2026-11-01_vetting/fill_recent_form.py (current QB = most-dropback starter of team's latest game;
  games = last 4 where player active (snaps>0 or pbp involvement) and that QB started).

## cross_checks (top level, pick-side only)
`cross_checks:[{name, url_or_file|source, pulled_et}]` — need a source and a parseable, non-future pulled_et; never satisfy a
gated category. PFF props live here (stamped 07:34 ET), not in `sources`.

## 2026-11-01 lessons audit additions
- `pff_inputs` (optional list): {leg, metric, value, scope, source, pulled_et, second_source:{name,value,source,pulled_et}, tolerance, pff_projection_side?, pff_matchup_side?}. Problems print under "PFF CROSS-CHECK (caution flags only; never a pass reason)" and don't change the exit code. scope weather/game_script/script/prop_projection/projection = FAIL.
- Runs dated >= 2026-11-05: every sims[].script must be tools/sim_v6.py. Live receiving legs also need pressure_inputs.time_to_throw and targets_under_pressure, each with a source and pulled_et.
- Weather alert placed legs: for dates other than 2026-11-01, they come from manifest `placed_legs`. If that's missing, the alert says "placed legs unknown".

## Rico 2026-11-01 (runs dated >= 2026-11-05)
- **Weather forecast days ahead (BUG-2026-11-01-WXDAYS):** the manifest needs `weather_forecast` (from `tools/weather_forecast.py`, written by `runs/2026-11-05_shared_src/assemble.py`), pulled no more than 24h earlier, with an entry for every game in the run. Open-air or unknown-roof games need status OK and numbers. The flag is recomputed (rain ≥50%, gusts ≥20, wind ≥15), and on a flag the passing/receiving OVERs must be CUT and a `WEATHER FORECAST ALERT` line prints. The Phase 11 pre-kick `weather` check stays the same.
- **Coverage profile on passing legs:** QB passing legs (market passyds/passcomp/completions/passtd/passatt, or a QB "pass" leg) need `coverage.man_zone` + `coverage.mof`, stamped at 48h, the same as receiving legs.

## Source-list rules (SRC-1..5, tools/srclist_rules.py)
- SRC-1 weather sources, weather blocks and weather_forecast providers must be NWS/Open-Meteo; PFF or anything else FAILS.
- SRC-2 pff_picks need edge_basis "our_model", book/book_line/book_price (odds age rule) and model_p for all 3 models; any PFF edge FAILS; pff_pick legs must sit at book_line.
- SRC-3 Sharp coverage source needs second_source {name (StatRankings/FTN/nflverse/pbp), url_or_file, pulled_et, agrees:true}; otherwise "SHARP CAUTION" (no fail) and legs citing Sharp coverage are BLOCKED from PRESS.
- SRC-5 (game_date >= 2026-11-05) manifest season/week + per-source season/data_week/pulled_et; wrong season, stale label week, or results data before week-1 FAILS. Pre-check: tools/feed_week_check.py.
